<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">United Democratic Party (Belize)</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1973–</span></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The United Democratic Party is one of the two main political parties of Belize, formed in 1973 by the merger of opposition groups. It has alternated in power with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peoples-united-party">People's United Party</a>, governing under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manuel-esquivel">Manuel Esquivel</a> in 1984–1989 and 1993–1998 and under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dean-barrow">Dean Barrow</a> from 2008 to 2020.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/united-democratic-party-belize.jpg" alt="United Democratic Party (Belize)" width="320" height="224" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: The original uploader was Fuebar at English Wikipedia. · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_the_Belize_United_Democratic_Party.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
